@node gpui-ui-kit User Guide
@section User Guide

End users experience this crate as every widget on screen: buttons,
sliders, menus, dialogs, knobs, meters. The look respects the active
theme (@ref{gpui-themes Manual}) and design system
(@ref{gpui-design Manual}).

@node gpui-ui-kit Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

@subheading Component groups

@table @asis
@item Core
@code{Button}, @code{IconButton}, @code{Card}, @code{Dialog},
@code{Menu}, @code{Tabs}, @code{Toast}.
@item Forms
@code{Input}, @code{NumberInput}, @code{Checkbox}, @code{Toggle},
@code{Select}, @code{Slider}, @code{ColorPicker}.
@item Data display
@code{Badge}, @code{Progress}, @code{Spinner}, @code{Avatar},
@code{Typography}.
@item Audio controls
@code{Potentiometer}, @code{VerticalSlider}, @code{VolumeKnob}.
@end table

@subheading Theming a component

@code{gpui-ui-kit-macros} provides @code{#[derive(ComponentTheme)]}
that generates @code{Default} and @code{From<&Theme>} impls for a
component theme struct.

@subheading Text input gotcha

@cindex text input
When using an @code{Input} inside a view that also defines
keybindings, ensure @code{is_input_editing()} is checked in
@code{is_text_input_mode()}. Without this guard, single-character keys
like @kbd{1} or @kbd{s} are intercepted by parent bindings instead of
being typed into the input.

